    $$def sum_digits(n):
    total = 0
    while n > 0:
        total += n % 10
    return total$$,
    $$def sum_digits(n):
    total = 0
    while n > 0:
        total += n % 10
        n //= 10
    return total$$,
    $$sum_digits(n) should add up the digits of a number, so sum_digits(123) gives 6.$$,
    $$Calling sum_digits(123) hangs and never returns.$$,
    $$The loop reads the last digit with n % 10 but never removes it, so n keeps its original value and the condition n > 0 stays true forever. Digit-extraction loops need both halves: read the last digit, then drop it with integer division. Any while loop should make you ask what changes the condition.$$,
    $$[{"input":[123],"expected_output":6},{"input":[9],"expected_output":9},{"input":[4070],"expected_output":11}]$$::jsonb,
    'published'
  )
  returning id
)
